(7655716, 1246438, 16912, '<td valign="top">Oh, I never thought about the cup handle but yes, I am left handed so well spotted. Yes, I like my Espresso but this was instant as I wasn''t going to let a decent coffee go cold lol. Francesca (my oh) prefers a ristretto but that would have had me bouncing off the walls.<br/> <br/>As for the light painting, the window was covered but still needed some ND filters to get things darker, then yes, grabbed my £3.99 torch with homemade snoot then painted away - it''s a really cool thing to try.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kasaba:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations - "non-hoarder" :-)) <br/>Did you flip this or are you left handed? :-) Or did it just look better this way? :-)))) And it looks like you drink "proper" coffee !!! <br/>Just curious, you shot this in the dark and used a torch to "paint" the light in? Very beautifully done. <br/>Lovely shot all round. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Oh, I never thought about the cup handle but yes, I am left handed so well spotted. Yes, I like my Espresso but this was instant as I wasn''t going to let a decent coffee go cold lol. Francesca (my oh) prefers a ristretto but that would have had me bouncing off the walls. As for the light painting, the window was covered but still needed some ND filters to get things darker, then yes, grabbed my £3.99 torch with homemade snoot then painted away - it''s a really cool thing to try. Originally posted by kasaba: Congratulations - "non-hoarder" :-)) Did you flip this or are you left handed? :-) Or did it just look better this way? :-)))) And it looks like you drink "proper" coffee !!! Just curious, you shot this in the dark and used a torch to "paint" the light in? Very beautifully done. Lovely shot all round. ', '2020-03-18 11:02:37.000000', NULL, 0),
